# 408 when analytics_manager tries to import to popular_queries ...
created: 2024-10-30, last updated: 2026-04-16, [Read more](https://github.com/typesense/typesense/issues/2040)

```
schema = {
"name": "customTestQueries",
"fields": [
{"name": "q", "type": "string" },
{"name": "count", "type": "int32" }
]
}
client.collections.create(schema)
ruleName = 'customTestQueriesAggregation'
ruleConfiguration = {
"type": "popular_queries",
"params": {
"source": {
"collections": ["customTest"]
},
"destination": {
"collection": "customTestQueries"
},
"expand_query": False,
"limit": 1000
}
}
client.analytics.rules.upsert(ruleName, ruleConfiguration)
```
...
`408` is a timeout status code.
The locally aggregated analytics data is sent to the leader (could be the same node in the case of a single node cluster) and this API call has a 4 second timeout.
...
found the issue.
analytics_manager was trying to use the wrong network.
setting the --peering-subnet argument correctly fixed the issue

